{"id":"a409ce5af84a094b669ef0df994d77bfdf63b32a","axis":"silent","repo":"vercel/turbo","sha":"a409ce5af84a094b669ef0df994d77bfdf63b32a","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"apps/docs/content/docs/reference/query.mdx","lines":["@@ -114,6 +114,16 @@ expanded names, framework-inferred variables, or a complete process environment."," The query does not execute tasks or report cache hits. Unlike dry-run summaries,"," this selection does not include file-hash inventories."," ","+## Package task catalogue","+","+`package.tasks` lists the package's native scripts and resolved Task Graph entries,","+including configured tasks without a script and tasks with an explicit command.","+Scriptless tasks can be entrypoints that depend on runnable tasks. Their `script`","+is `null`, and their `command` is `null` unless a command is configured. Inherited","+and shared configurations are resolved before listing tasks; scriptless tasks","+excluded by `extends: false` are not included. Task names are deduplicated and sorted.","+Task filters apply to this full catalogue, not only tasks with native scripts.","+"," ## Tags"," "," Packages and tasks expose a `tags` array, returning `[]` when no labels are configured. Package tags come from the package's loaded `turbo.json` and do not include task labels or inherit root package labels.","@@ -137,7 +147,7 @@ query {"," '"," ```"," ","-Task predicates support `and`, `or`, and `not`, as well as `equal` and `notEqual` on `NAME` and `FULL_NAME`. The optional task `filter` is available on package task lists, task dependency/dependent lists, and `withDependencies`.","+Task predicates support `and`, `or`, and `not`, as well as `equal` and `notEqual` on `NAME`, `FULL_NAME`, and `EXPERIMENTAL_CI`. `EXPERIMENTAL_CI` compares the resolved `experimentalCI` metadata as JSON: a boolean, an object, or `null` when unset. Objects use structural equality, not partial matching. An omitted predicate `value` is equivalent to explicit `null`. `NAME` and `FULL_NAME` equality still only matches strings, and `TAG` membership still only matches string labels. To select configured values other than `false`, combine `notEqual: {field: EXPERIMENTAL_CI, value: null}` and `notEqual: {field: EXPERIMENTAL_CI, value: false}` with `and`. This comparison does not interpret metadata contents or assign meaning to tags. The optional task `filter` is available on package task lists, task dependency/dependent lists, and `withDependencies`."," "," For affected tasks, pass `taskFilter` alongside the existing package `filter` or task-name `tasks` arguments:"," "],"additions":11,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"crates/turborepo-query/src/affected_tasks.rs","lines":["@@ -236,7 +236,7 @@ mod tests {","     use turborepo_ui::ColorConfig;"," ","     use super::*;","-    use crate::QueryRun;","+    use crate::{Package, QueryRun};"," ","     struct MockDiscovery;"," ","@@ -649,7 +649,7 @@ mod tests {","     }"," ","     #[tokio::test]","-    async fn injected_go_graph_queries_packages_tasks_and_aggregate_exclusion() {","+    async fn injected_go_graph_queries_packages_tasks_and_scriptless_aggregate_entries() {","         let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();","         let root = AbsoluteSystemPath::from_std_path(tmp.path()).unwrap();","         let graph = PackageGraph::builder_optional(root, None)","@@ -708,9 +708,15 @@ mod tests {","                 .len(),","             2","         );","-        // Even with an engine build node, the Go aggregate's contract task","-        // does not register module-only build/test commands on this scope.","-        assert_eq!(workspace[\"tasks\"][\"items\"], serde_json::json!([]));","+        // The injected engine entry is visible, but does not invent a native","+        // module-only build command or a test task for this aggregate scope.","+        assert_eq!(","+            workspace[\"tasks\"][\"items\"],","+            serde_json::json!([{","+                \"name\": \"build\", \"fullName\": \"go-worksp